From 7712aa97dac2598e37c3ecc82b2a2e1bedec5776 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frederik Richter <frederik.richter@mailbox.org>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:25:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(config/render): unify sdr and hdr brightness settings in
 monitor definition

Hyprland 0.57 port: the legacy hyprlang config manager (and with it the
monitor/monitorv2 keyword handling) is gone and config is Lua-only, HyprCtl
moved to src/ipc/s1/Commands.cpp, the renderer got a CRenderContext and the
blur implementation moved to src/render/gl/blur/Kawase.cpp.

- Add hdrbrightness monitor rule setting to scale HDR content brightness on HDR monitors
- Add unified brightness monitor rule setting to adjust both SDR and HDR brightness simultaneously
- Add Lua config bindings for brightness, sdrbrightness and hdrbrightness
- Fix HDR surface brightness scaling in Renderer getCMSettings and OpenGL renderToFBInternal by recognizing the EXT_LINEAR work buffer on HDR monitors
- Support Windows scRGB / extended linear surfaces in HDR surface detection
- Ensure skipCM does not bypass the CM shader when brightness/saturation modifications are active, while keeping the 0.57 EXPLICIT_SCENE scene-resource optimization intact
- Preserve monitor rule output name when falling back to active monitor rule in Lua hl.monitor
- Expose brightness, sdr_brightness, and hdr_brightness on Lua HL.Monitor object (resolving active brightness based on HDR state)
- Avoid redundant applyCMType calls in applyMonitorRuleSoft while ensuring immediate monitor damage and blur invalidation on brightness change
- Fix direct scanout bypassing HDR and SDR brightness scaling
- Fix min brightness (0.0) making the screen completely black instead of jumping to 100%
- Guard blurprepare against division by zero when brightness is zero
- Validate non-negative and finite brightness values in parsers and bindings
- Expose hdrBrightness in hyprctl monitors JSON and text outputs
- Expand unit test coverage in tests/config/MonitorParser.cpp
---

